  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 052344\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 PM HST Thu Nov 05 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nEastern Central Pacific (CP95):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with an area of low pressure\nlocated several hundred miles to the southeast of the Big Island of\nHawaii continue to show signs of organization, though recent\nsatellite wind data indicate the system lacks a well-defined center.\nEnvironmental conditions are conducive for additional development,\nand a tropical depression is expected to develop by early Friday.\nThe system is forecast to move west-northwestward to westward at 10\nto 15 mph, passing well south of the Hawaiian Islands.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...90 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Evans/Blake\nNNNN",
